nding","priority":"high"},{"content":"Implement data_loader (all 6 CSVs)","status":"pending","priority":"high"},{"content":"Implement queries (matches, teams, players, competitions, stats)","status":"pending","priority":"high"},{"content":"Implement FastMCP server with tools","status":"pending","priority":"high"},{"content":"Write pytest-bdd GWT tests","status":"pending","priority":"high"},{"content":"Run tests, fix issues, update README","status":"pending","priority":"high"}],"truncated":false},"title":"7 todos","time":{"start":1782090199092,"end":1782090199098}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The guide is essentially the same as TASK.md. Let me plan the implementation.\n\nPlan:\n1. Create a Python package `brazilian_soccer_mcp/` with:\n   - `data_loader.py` - loads and normalizes all CSVs\n   - `normalizers.py` - team name normalization, date parsing\n   - `queries.py` - query functions for matches, teams, players, competitions, statistics\n   - `server.py` - FastMCP server exposing tools\n2. `pyproject.toml` or `setup.py` for build\n3. `tests/` with pytest-bdd GWT tests\n4. `conftest.py`\n5. README update\n\nLet me design carefully. I'll use fastmcp since it's installed. Let me write everything.\n\nLet me start with the data loader and normalizers.\n\nKey normalization: team names like \"Palmeiras-SP\" → \"Palmeiras\". \"Flamengo-RJ\" → \"Flamengo\". Also handle \"América - MG\", \"Sport Club Corinthians Paulista\". I'll create a canonical name function that strips state suffixes (e.g., \"-SP\", \"-RJ\", \" - MG\"), and a function to compute a normalized key (lowercase, no accents, no spaces, no state).\n\nLet me check team name formats in Brazilian_Cup_Matches: \"Boavista Sport Club (antigo Esporte Clube Barreira) - RJ\", \"América - MG\". So format uses \" - RJ\" separator. Brasileirão uses \"-SP\" suffix without spaces.\n\nDate formats: ISO \"2023-09-24\", \"2012-05-19 18:30:00\", \"29/03/2003\" (DD/MM/YYYY).\n\nLet me write the normalizer carefully.\n\nFor team name normalization, I'll:\n1. Strip trailing state suffix patterns: `-XX` at end, ` - XX` at end.\n2. Lowercase, remove accents, strip non-alphanumeric for matching key.\n\nBrazilian states: AC, AL, AP, AM, BA, CE, DF, ES, GO, MA, MT, MS, MG, PA, PB, PR, PE, PI, RJ, RN, RS, RO, RR, SC, SP, SE, TO.\n\nI'll write a regex to strip `[-\\s]+[A-Z]{2}$` from the cleaned team name.\n\nLet me build the code now. I'll create a clean modular structure.\n\nStructure:\n- `brazilian_soccer_mcp/__init__.py`\n- `brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalizers.py`\n- `brazilian_soccer_mcp/data_loader.py`\n- `brazilian_soccer_mcp/queries.py`\n- `brazilian_soccer_mcp/server.py`\n- `pyproject.toml`\n- `tests/conftest.py`\n- `tests/test_normalizers.py`\n- `tests/test_data_loader.py`\n- `tests/test_queries.py`\n- `tests/features/match_queries.feature`\n- `tests/test_bdd.py`\n\nLet me write these. I'll make the context block comment at the start of every code file as the prompts suggest.\n\nLet me write the normalizer first.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_eecda643a001obA8eZ5Aj4B75W","sessionID":"ses_11326b3aaffebuPmo4MbnyTU6H","messageID":"msg_eecda3fc6001u86S4xCOkCd3Tu"}}
