{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1782090396642,"sessionID":"ses_11326b3aaffebuPmo4MbnyTU6H","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-ae30221309499fec","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-gmuuihfv/retort-aaf587c63f9c/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalizers.py","newString":"def normalize_competition(name: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Map raw competition/tournament labels to a canonical competition name.\n\n    The BR-Football-Dataset uses ad-hoc tournament strings (\"Serie A\",\n    \"Copa do Brasil\", ...). We map those to the canonical labels used across\n    the other files so cross-file queries work consistently.\n\n    >>> normalize_competition(\"Serie A\")\n    'Brasileirao'\n    >>> normalize_competition(\"Copa do Brasil\")\n    'Copa do Brasil'\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(name, str):\n        return \"Unknown\"\n    key = re.sub(r\"\\s+\", \" \", strip_accents(name).lower()).strip()\n    if key in {\"serie a\", \"brasileirao serie a\", \"brasileirao\"}:\n        return \"Brasileirao\"\n    if key in {\"serie b\", \"brasileirao serie b\"}:\n        return \"Serie B\"\n    if key in {\"serie c\", \"brasileirao serie c\"}:\n        return \"Serie C\"\n    if key in {\"copa do brasil\", \"brazilian cup\"}:\n        return \"Copa do Brasil\"\n    if key in {\"libertadores\", \"copa libertadores\", \"copa libertadores da america\"}:\n        return \"Copa Libertadores\"\n    if key in {\"sulamericana\", \"copa sudamericana\"}:\n        return \"Copa Sudamericana\"\n    # Fallback: return the original cleaned name (title-cased).\n    return name.strip()\n\n\ndef to_int(value, default=0) -> int:","oldString":"def to_int(value, default=0) -> int:"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-gmuuihfv/retort-aaf587c63f9c/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalizers.py\n===================================================================\n--- /private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-gmuuihfv/retort-aaf587c63f9c/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalizers.py\n+++ /private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-gmuuihfv/retort-aaf587c63f9c/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalizers.py\n@@ -141,8 +141,39 @@\n     except ValueError:\n         return None\n \n \n+def normalize_competition(name: str) -> str:\n+    \"\"\"Map raw competition/tournament labels to a canonical competition name.\n+\n+    The BR-Football-Dataset uses ad-hoc tournament strings (\"Serie A\",\n+    \"Copa do Brasil\", ...). We map those to the canonical labels used across\n+    the other files so cross-file queries work consistently.\n+\n+    >>> normalize_competition(\"Serie A\")\n+    'Brasileirao'\n+    >>> normalize_competition(\"Copa do Brasil\")\n+    'Copa do Brasil'\n+    \"\"\"\n+    if not isinstance(name, str):\n+        return \"Unknown\"\n+    key = re.sub(r\"\\s+\", \" \", strip_accents(name).lower()).strip()\n+    if key in {\"serie a\", \"brasileirao serie a\", \"brasileirao\"}:\n+        return \"Brasileirao\"\n+    if key in {\"serie b\", \"brasileirao serie b\"}:\n+        return \"Serie B\"\n+    if key in {\"serie c\", \"brasileirao serie c\"}:\n+        return \"Serie C\"\n+    if key in {\"copa do brasil\", \"brazilian cup\"}:\n+        return \"Copa do Brasil\"\n+    if key in {\"libertadores\", \"copa libertadores\", \"copa libertadores da america\"}:\n+        return \"Copa Libertadores\"\n+    if key in {\"sulamericana\", \"copa sudamericana\"}:\n+        return \"Copa Sudamericana\"\n+    # Fallback: return the original cleaned name (title-cased).\n+    return name.strip()\n+\n+\n def to_int(value, default=0) -> int:\n     \"\"\"Best-effort conversion of a goal/corner cell to int. Handles '2', 2.0, ''.\"\"\"\n     if value is None:\n         return default\n","filediff":{"file":"/private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-gmuuihfv/retort-aaf587c63f9c/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalizers.py","patch":"Index: /private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-gmuuihfv/retort-aaf587c63f9c/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalizers.py\n===================================================================\n--- /private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-gmuuihfv/retort-aaf587c63f9c/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalizers.py\n+++ /private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-gmuuihfv/retort-aaf587c63f9c/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalizers.py\n@@ -141,8 +141,39 @@\n     except ValueError:\n         return None\n \n \n+def normalize_competition(name: str) -> str:\n+    \"\"\"Map raw competition/tournament labels to a canonical competition name.\n+\n+    The BR-Football-Dataset uses ad-hoc tournament strings (\"Serie A\",\n+    \"Copa do Brasil\", ...). We map those to the canonical labels used across\n+    the other files so cross-file queries work consistently.\n+\n+    >>> normalize_competition(\"Serie A\")\n+    'Brasileirao'\n+    >>> normalize_competition(\"Copa do Brasil\")\n+    'Copa do Brasil'\n+    \"\"\"\n+    if not isinstance(name, str):\n+        return \"Unknown\"\n+    key = re.sub(r\"\\s+\", \" \", strip_accents(name).lower()).strip()\n+    if key in {\"serie a\", \"brasileirao serie a\", \"brasileirao\"}:\n+        return \"Brasileirao\"\n+    if key in {\"serie b\", \"brasileirao serie b\"}:\n+        return \"Serie B\"\n+    if key in {\"serie c\", \"brasileirao serie c\"}:\n+        return \"Serie C\"\n+    if key in {\"copa do brasil\", \"brazilian cup\"}:\n+        return \"Copa do Brasil\"\n+    if key in {\"libertadores\", \"copa libertadores\", \"copa libertadores da america\"}:\n+        return \"Copa Libertadores\"\n+    if key in {\"sulamericana\", \"copa sudamericana\"}:\n+        return \"Copa Sudamericana\"\n+    # Fallback: return the original cleaned name (title-cased).\n+    return name.strip()\n+\n+\n def to_int(value, default=0) -> int:\n     \"\"\"Best-effort conversion of a goal/corner cell to int. Handles '2', 2.0, ''.\"\"\"\n     if value is None:\n         return default\n","additions":31,"deletions":0},"truncated":false},"title":"brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalizers.py","time":{"start":1782090396638,"end":1782090396640}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"So Brasileirao_Matches.csv only goes to 2022. Flamengo 2023 = 0 is correct (no 2023 data in Brasileirao file). But BR-Football-Dataset has 2023 with tournament \"Serie A\". The user querying \"Brasileirao\" 2023 wouldn't match \"Serie A\". \n\nThat's fine - it's a data limitation. But the champion 2019 doubled-counted because both Brasileirao_Matches and novo_campeonato_brasileiro have 2019. The historical CSV ends in 2019, and the modern Brasileirao starts 2012. So 2012-2019 overlap is double-counted.\n\nI should dedupe. Actually the task says \"All 6 CSV files are loadable and queryable\" and \"Cross-file queries work\". Double-counting is a real data quality issue. For standings I should probably treat them as separate competitions. The historical one is labeled \"Brasileirao (2003-2019)\" which is distinct from \"Brasileirao\". But champion('Brasileirao', 2019) matches both because \"brasileirao\" is substring of \"brasileirao (2003-2019)\".\n\nI should use exact match for competition filtering rather than substring. But the BR-Football-Dataset has tournament=\"Serie A\" which should map to Brasileirao. Hmm.\n\nLet me reconsider. Better approach: normalize competition labels. Map \"Serie A\" → \"Brasileirao\". And keep historical separate. And use exact matching (case-insensitive) for competition, with a synonym map.\n\nLet me add a competition normalization function. Synonyms:\n- \"Serie A\", \"Brasileirao Serie A\" → \"Brasileirao\"\n- \"Copa do Brasil\" stays\n- \"Libertadores\", \"Copa Libertadores\" → \"Copa Libertadores\"\n\nAnd for querying, exact match on normalized competition. Then champion('Brasileirao', 2019) only matches Brasileirao (modern) → 38 matches, not 76. And historical is queried as \"Brasileirao (2003-2019)\".\n\nLet me add a normalize_competition function in normalizers and use it both at load time (for the BR-Football-Dataset tournament column) and in queries (for the filter). Actually, simpler: store a `competition` already normalized at load, and in queries do exact case-insensitive match.\n\nBut the BR-Football-Dataset has many tournament values (Serie A, Serie B, Copa do Brasil, etc.). Let me normalize all of them.\n\nLet me add normalize_competition.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_eecdd68e1001egIAREH6F23MVH","sessionID":"ses_11326b3aaffebuPmo4MbnyTU6H","messageID":"msg_eecdd45120018PtEo2dVAC3izn"}}
