{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1782090515171,"sessionID":"ses_11326b3aaffebuPmo4MbnyTU6H","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_5a8cf00e686b43b9b3841703","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"python3 -c \"\nfrom brazilian_soccer_mcp import DataLoader\nloader=DataLoader()\n# Flamengo 2022 Brasileirao from BR-Football-Dataset\nrows=[m for m in loader.matches if m.competition=='Brasileirao' and m.season==2022 and m.source_file=='BR-Football-Dataset.csv' and (m.home_team_key=='flamengo' or m.away_team_key=='flamengo')]\nfor m in rows[:5]:\n    print(m.date, m.home_team, m.away_team, m.home_goals, m.away_goals)\nprint('---brasileirao_matches---')\nrows2=[m for m in loader.matches if m.competition=='Brasileirao' and m.season==2022 and m.source_file=='Brasileirao_Matches.csv' and (m.home_team_key=='flamengo')]\nfor m in rows2[:5]:\n    print(m.date, m.home_team, m.away_team, m.home_goals, m.away_goals)\n\"","description":"Compare Flamengo match records across sources"},"output":"2022-11-12 00:00:00 Flamengo Avai 1 2\n2022-11-10 00:00:00 EC Juventude Flamengo 2 2\n2022-11-06 00:00:00 Coritiba Flamengo 1 0\n2022-11-03 00:00:00 Flamengo Corinthians 1 2\n2022-10-26 00:00:00 Flamengo Santos 3 2\n---brasileirao_matches---\n2022-04-17 16:00:00 Flamengo Sao Paulo 3 1\n2022-04-20 19:30:00 Flamengo Palmeiras 0 0\n2022-05-08 11:00:00 Flamengo Botafogo 0 1\n2022-05-21 16:30:00 Flamengo Goias 1 0\n2022-06-05 16:00:00 Flamengo Fortaleza 1 2\n","metadata":{"output":"2022-11-12 00:00:00 Flamengo Avai 1 2\n2022-11-10 00:00:00 EC Juventude Flamengo 2 2\n2022-11-06 00:00:00 Coritiba Flamengo 1 0\n2022-11-03 00:00:00 Flamengo Corinthians 1 2\n2022-10-26 00:00:00 Flamengo Santos 3 2\n---brasileirao_matches---\n2022-04-17 16:00:00 Flamengo Sao Paulo 3 1\n2022-04-20 19:30:00 Flamengo Palmeiras 0 0\n2022-05-08 11:00:00 Flamengo Botafogo 0 1\n2022-05-21 16:30:00 Flamengo Goias 1 0\n2022-06-05 16:00:00 Flamengo Fortaleza 1 2\n","exit":0,"description":"Compare Flamengo match records across sources","truncated":false},"title":"Compare Flamengo match records across sources","time":{"start":1782090515102,"end":1782090515170}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Two findings:\n1. FIFA data has very few Brazilian clubs (mostly European). \"Grêmio\", \"Atlético Mineiro\" present but no \"Flamengo\". So `players_at_club('Flamengo')` returns 0 legitimately — the FIFA dataset just doesn't include Flamengo players. That's a data limitation, not a bug. But team_key(\"Atlético Mineiro\") — does it match? Our override maps \"atletico mineiro\" → \"Atletico-MG\". And team_key for club \"Atlético Mineiro\" → strip accents \"Atletico Mineiro\" → lowercase → \"atletico mineiro\" → override → \"atletico mg\". And team_key(\"Atlético Mineiro\" as query) → same. So players_at_club('Atlético Mineiro') would work. But \"Flamengo\" isn't in FIFA data. Fine.\n\nActually wait, the FIFA data is from FIFA games which historically didn't have Brazilian club licenses. So Brazilian clubs are mostly absent. That's expected. The `players_at_club` tool still works for clubs that ARE present. Good.\n\n2. Dedup didn't fully collapse: 38 + 25 = 63, but dedup should have removed the 25 overlapping ones. Why? The 25 BR-Football-Dataset entries that remain must have different (date, home_key, away_key, score) than the 38 Brasileirao_Matches entries. Possibly because BR-Football-Dataset has different home/away team naming producing different keys, OR the scores differ, OR dates differ.\n\nLet me investigate one.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_eecdf3c8d001YBAHh1fzd1kTJB","sessionID":"ses_11326b3aaffebuPmo4MbnyTU6H","messageID":"msg_eecdf05100012h26VxbuZ7KSJX"}}
