es)","status":"completed","priority":"high"},{"content":"Implement data_loader (all 6 CSVs)","status":"completed","priority":"high"},{"content":"Implement queries (matches, teams, players, competitions, stats)","status":"completed","priority":"high"},{"content":"Implement FastMCP server with tools","status":"completed","priority":"high"},{"content":"Write pytest-bdd GWT tests","status":"in_progress","priority":"high"},{"content":"Run tests, fix issues, update README","status":"pending","priority":"high"}],"truncated":false},"title":"2 todos","time":{"start":1782090533181,"end":1782090533182}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The dedup uses `m.date.date().isoformat()`. For Brasileirao_Matches, dates have times → date is e.g. \"2022-04-17\". For BR-Football-Dataset, date \"2022-11-12\". These should both produce date-only ISO. So the date key matches when the same match.\n\nBut the home/away team: BR-Football-Dataset \"Avai\" → team_key \"avai\". Brasileirao_Matches \"Avaí-SC\"? → strip accents \"Avai\" → key \"avai\". Should match.\n\nThe Flamengo Avai 1-2 in BR-Football-Dataset (2022-11-12). Is there a corresponding Brasileirao_Matches entry with same date and score? Let me check. Actually maybe the Brasileirao_Matches Flamengo-Avai was a different score or date. These datasets are independent; the BR-Football-Dataset might have errors or the match genuinely appears once in each but with slightly different data. \n\nActually — maybe Brasileirao_Matches 2022 doesn't include Avai match, or the score differs. The dedup is correct: only removes EXACT same (date, teams, score). The 25 remaining are genuinely non-identical records. That's a real data inconsistency.\n\nThis is acceptable for a demo. The double-count concern is largely resolved — we removed exact duplicates. Remaining differences reflect genuine data discrepancies between sources. I'll leave it. Actually, the dedup removed 1221 matches (23954 → 22733). Good enough.\n\nLet me move on to tests. The behavior is acceptable. Let me write BDD tests.\n\nNow let me write tests with pytest-bdd GWT structure.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_eecdf891b001zQqrl47suJbAkt","sessionID":"ses_11326b3aaffebuPmo4MbnyTU6H","messageID":"msg_eecdf43910019woe7K1GTfGHu2"}}
